From: MGS2 RG353VS compatibility port
Subject: [PATCH] windecode: never touch a DirectShow graph that was not created

Independent of the wpatch records. Apply to the recovered game source; the
file has CRCRLF endings, so use `patch --binary`.

WindowsMpegInit() only logs a failed CoCreateInstance(CLSID_FilterGraph) and
returns, leaving WindowsMpegWork zeroed. Nothing downstream tests for that.
MpegDecFirstRend() calls RCTInit() -- which dereferences WindowsMpegWork.pGB
unconditionally -- BEFORE it checks WindowsMpegInitFlag, and WinstrmSendIPic()
dereferences WindowsMpegWork.pSrcFTR and pSrcFTRInPin with no check at all.

In the shipping port executable this is not hypothetical: WindowsMpegInit() is
stubbed with `ret` at VA 0x00878FE0, so pGB is NULL for the life of the
process while the in-memory movie consumer still reaches WinstrmSendIPic().
Measured on the device 2026-08-31 03:04, in ordinary play about 2.5 minutes
after the first frame:

    wine: Unhandled page fault on read access to 00000000 at address 0087AE0F
    (thread 0100), starting debugger...

0x0087AE0F is `mov ecx,[eax]` in RCTInit with eax = WindowsMpegWork.pGB = 0,
reached from 0x00888803 -> WinstrmSendIPic -> MpegDecFirstRend -> RCTInit.
wine exited 5 and the session ended.

Moving the existing WindowsMpegInitFlag test above RCTInit() closes the
measured fault, the new WinstrmSendIPic() test closes the second dereference
one instruction later at 0x0087A7E0 (WindowsMpegWork.pSrcFTR), and the two
clock guards make RCTInit/RCTRelease safe on their own terms rather than by
the caller's ordering.

The bounded equivalent in the hash-pinned temporary image is two bytes, both
`ret` at a function entry, which is what FINALPLAY23 applies:

    offset 4696000  VA 0x0087A7C0  WinstrmSendIPic  53 -> c3
    offset 4697600  VA 0x0087AE00  RCTInit          51 -> c3

Neither is a behaviour change while the init stub stands: no movie played
before this patch and none plays after it. Restoring movie playback is a
separate, still-open problem -- see docs/MGS2_PROJECT_STATE.md section 6d.

--- a/mgs2x/source/game/windecode.cpp
+++ b/mgs2x/source/game/windecode.cpp
@@ -1119,14 +1119,14 @@
 {
 	HRESULT hr = S_OK;
 	
-#if TRUE 
-	RCTInit() ;
-#endif
-
 	if(!WindowsMpegWork.WindowsMpegInitFlag){
 		return(hr);
 	}
 
+#if TRUE 
+	RCTInit() ;
+#endif
+
 	if (FAILED(hr = WindowsMpegWork.pMC->Run()))
 	{
 		Msg(TEXT("Could not run the DirectShow graph44!  hr=0x%x"), hr);
@@ -2018,6 +2018,9 @@
 	
 	
 	int	rc;
+	if(!WindowsMpegWork.WindowsMpegInitFlag){
+		return(0);
+	}
 	if(mp2 -> init_flag){
 	}else{
 		IReferenceClock	*rclk;
@@ -2451,7 +2454,7 @@
 static	void	RCTInit(void)
 {
 	IMediaFilter	*pMF ;
-	if( !_pRCTest_set )
+	if( !_pRCTest_set && WindowsMpegWork.pGB )
 	{
 		WindowsMpegWork.pGB->QueryInterface(IID_IMediaFilter,(void **)&pMF);
 		pMF->SetSyncSource(&_pRCTest) ;
@@ -2463,7 +2466,7 @@
 static	void	RCTRelease(void)
 {
 	IMediaFilter	*pMF ;
-	if( _pRCTest_set )
+	if( _pRCTest_set && WindowsMpegWork.pGB )
 	{
 		printf("RCT Release\n");
